  "difference_complete_minus_extend": 0.00744,
  "counts": {
   "EXTEND_no_new_pair": 387755,
   "COMPLETE_increases_matched": 356016
  },
  "VERDICT": "C4 not refuted on this split (CIs overlap)",
  "interpretation_if_complete_is_dearer": "Then the mechanism is: accumulate the first leg cheaply while it stays cheap, then PAY UP to close the pair. That is a two-state conditional policy -- cheap accumulation plus willingness-to-complete -- and it is exactly the component a static-cap clone would omit."
